WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:05.470
This year's edition of San Diego Comic-Con
was a slightly more subdued affair than usual.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.550
Amidst much of the usual hype for all things
geeky, both Marvel Studios and HBO skipped

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:11.900
the event entirely.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:17.119
Still, even with those two powerhouses missing,
there was plenty to talk about - both good

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.119
and bad.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:23.200
Here's a look at the 4 best and 4 worst reveals
at San Diego Comic-Con 2018.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.320
Best: The Shazam! Trailer

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.120
DC's slate of superhero films have been criticized
in the past for being too dark and serious.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.050
Well, it seems like Warner Bros. was listening,
because the first trailer for Shazam! was

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.000
an unbridled joy, full of fun and laughs.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.230
From pop culture references to star Zachary
Levi's wide-eyed glee as a boy stuck in a

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:45.710
superhero's body, everything about Shazam!
was pitch perfect, making it one of the best

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:48.370
debuts in recent Comic-Con history.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.670
Worst: Bumblebee's baddie

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.640
Generally speaking, the Transformers prequel
Bumblebee looks like it's heading in the right

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.620
direction, with a scaled down story and more
human-sized emotional content.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.210
But fans were gravely disappointed when director
Travis Knight revealed at a Comic-Con panel

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:07.640
that the flying Decepticon in the trailer
is not who fans hoped and expected it to be,

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:08.400
saying

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.000
"I'm gonna break a few hearts here today.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.400
It is not Starscream."

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.620
Instead, it turns out the bad guy is actually
Blitzwing, a Decepticon who just happens to

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:19.410
look a lot like the fan favorite villain Starscream.

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:23.740
It seems kind of like a mean trick, but then
again, should we really be surprised at deception

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.900
from a Decepticon?

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.050
Best: The Aquaman trailer

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:31.800
Described as Star Wars set beneath the sea,
and led by a dazzling cast featuring Jason

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.690
Momoa, Nicole Kidman, Patrick Wilson, and
Amber Heard, Aquaman wasn't just one of Warner

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:41.650
Bros.' most anticipated reveals at this year's
SDCC, it was also one of its best.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:46.490
Between Momoa's Aquaman facing off with Wilson's
villainous, shark-riding Orm to become the

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:52.060
rightful ruler of Atlantis and all those breathtaking
underwater set pieces, the Aquaman trailer

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.540
was, as The Hollywood Reporter put it, the
best received at Comic-Con.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.850
Our appetite has definitely been whet.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.560
"That was the worst pep talk, ever."

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.750
Worst: The James Gunn double whammy

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.990
Even though Marvel Studios skipped Comic-Con,
they still managed to make the biggest headlines

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.450
- but not in a good way.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:13.110
On Friday, July 20th, the second day of Comic-Con,
it was announced that writer and director

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:18.590
James Gunn had been fired from Guardians of
the Galaxy Vol. 3 after a conservative website

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:22.350
unearthed some controversial tweets Gunn posted
prior to landing his gig with Marvel.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.930
Gunn had been scheduled to appear at Sony's
Comic-Con panel later that evening to announce

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.750
a secret project, but in the wake of his firing,
that appearance was cancelled as well, leaving

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.080
the status of the project up in the air.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.180
Gunn getting fired and then not appearing
at SDCC was a twofold shocker one Twitter

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.930
user best summed up: "It's crazy that the
only thing the MCU brought to Comic-Con this

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.220
year was the firing of James Gunn."

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.120
Best: The Glass trailer

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.650
Nearly two decades after his 2000 hit Unbreakable,
director M. Night Shyamalan finally unveiled

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:58.090
the trailer for the long awaited sequel, Glass,
which also acts as a follow-up to 2017's Split.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.950
Stylish, wonderfully self-aware, sprinkled
with action, and featuring Sarah Paulson as

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.380
a psychiatrist who specializes in treating
super-powered people, Glass looks to be an

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.840
ambitious return to form.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.060
We can't wait to see how it all turns out.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.500
Worst: The Johnny Depp debacle

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.930
After unleashing a magical trailer for Fantastic
Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald, Warner

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:22.590
Bros. gave Comic-Con a rollicking good time,
with a panel featuring stars Jude Law and

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.700
Ezra Miller.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.990
Unfortunately, those good times turned a little
sour when embattled actor Johnny Depp showed

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.450
up in full costume as the villainous Gellert
Grindelwald.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:35.670
Appearing to a very mixed reaction of cheers
and boos, Depp pressed forward with a pre-written

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.670
monologue.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:40.680
But for some fans, the appearance was particularly
jarring given his ex-wife Amber Heard, who

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.220
famously accused Depp of domestic abuse, appeared
on the same stage less than two hours later

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.849
to promote Aquaman.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:49.920
Reaction online was particularly negative,
with one Twitter user writing,

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.800
"The fact that the audience didn't boo Johnny
Depp off the stage at Comic-Con highly disappoints

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.720
me."

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:57.240
Best: Star Wars: The Clone Wars lives!

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.860
"A war left unfinished… until now."

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:04.099
Those six words sent attendees at this year's
San Diego Comic-Con into fits of unbridled

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:08.430
joy, as Disney and Lucasfilm announced the
return of the fan favorite animated series

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:12.200
Star Wars: The Clone Wars, which Disney had
abruptly cancelled when they acquired the

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:14.950
rights to Star Wars way back in 2013.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:19.840
Now fans finally will get their wish, as Clone
Wars supervising director Dave Filoni said

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.759
that the 12-episode revival, which is set
to debut on Disney's upcoming new streaming

00:04:23.759 --> 00:04:28.229
service, only happened because of viewers'
relentless enthusiasm and support.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.080
Turns out anything is truly possible with
The Force.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.000
Worst: Bye-bye, Rick

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:38.090
In May, 2018, fans of the wildly popular TV
series The Walking Dead were thrown for a

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:42.309
loop when reports began swirling that Andrew
Lincoln, who plays lead Rick Grimes, would

00:04:42.309 --> 00:04:45.629
be leaving the show for good during the show's
upcoming ninth season.

00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:49.900
Lincoln, however, remained mum, leading some
fans to hope that maybe those reports were

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:50.900
wrong.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:54.150
Unfortunately, though, Lincoln dashed those
hopes during his appearance at Comic-Con,

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.449
telling bereaved fans that he was indeed quitting.

00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:59.800
"This will be my last season playing the part
of Rick Grimes.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:04.300
This has been the most extraordinary, amazing,
and beautiful experience of my career […] These

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.540
guys here [...] are the greatest surrogate
family I could have wished for.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.200
But I do have a real family, and it's time
for me to go home."

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.760
We're not crying, you are.

